# Documentation review

Whenever you make a change, review and update documentation that the change touches. Do this in the same change unless the user explicitly says not to.

| Surface | When to update |
| --- | --- |
| **README** (`README.md`) | Setup, configuration, environment variables, API surface, CLI usage, or anything else a reader would expect there. Skip when the change does not affect what the README documents. |
| **OpenAPI** | Any HTTP contract change: route `summary` / `description` / `response_description`, query and path parameter descriptions, Pydantic response and request models (`Field` descriptions, examples, schema titles). FastAPI serves the schema at `GET /api/v1/openapi.json`; keep route and schema metadata accurate so generated docs stay correct. |
| **Docstrings** | Module, function, and method docstrings for code you add or whose contract you change (parameters, return value, side effects, raised exceptions). Follow Google-style docstrings per `python-standards.mdc`. |

# Tests for new functionality

When you add new functionality (routes, services, core behavior, or other user-facing or contract-changing behavior), add or extend automated tests in the same change so the new behavior is covered, unless the user explicitly says not to.
